From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: media: cedrus: the H713 video engine runs at 432 MHz only while the AV1 decoder is on

0293 holds the H713's video engine at 432 MHz because the AV1 core, which
runs from the same module clock, stalls into its own timeout above that.
Since 0310 the AV1 decoder is off, and nothing else asked for 432 MHz:
cedrus ran its own codecs 28 % below the 600 MHz of the H6 variant whose
compatible the H713 binds. At 432 MHz H.264 2160p decodes at 26 frames/s
alone, and under Kodi HEVC 2160p30 reached 28.4 to 28.8 frames/s, so 4K
did not play smoothly.

The rate is now chosen at probe: 432 MHz while an enabled
"allwinner,sun50i-h713-av1" node is in the device tree, the variant's
600 MHz otherwise. Bringing the AV1 decoder back (dropping 0310) brings
the 432 MHz back with it, and the AV1 driver still refuses to probe
above 432 MHz. One line at probe names the rate.

Measured on the HY310, 15.10.2026, the kernel before this patch against
the kernel with it (a warm start between, the same userspace); under
load the CCU reads PLL_VE at 432 MHz before and 600 MHz after:

 - decoding alone (GStreamer into fakevideosink, wall clock with the
   pipeline's start): H.264 2160p 24.3 -> 28.6 frames/s, HEVC 2160p
   8 bit 49.0 -> 55.4 and 10 bit 43.3 -> 49.2, H.264 1080p 105 -> 129,
   VP9 1080p60 189 -> 219;
 - mpv, H.264 2160p30: 26.6 -> 30.0 frames/s out of the engine; HEVC
   2160p30 30.0 at both rates;
 - Kodi, H.264 2160p30 (a 10 s clip in a loop): 24.8 -> 27.6 frames/s
   over a minute, 5 s windows at most 27.4 before and up to 30.0 after,
   skipped frames 174 -> 70. HEVC 2160p30 stays at 28.6 frames/s: between
   the loop's restarts it runs at 30.0 at either rate, so that clip loses
   its frames to the restart and not to the engine;
 - bit-exact at 600 MHz: the 33 clips of the decoder suite (H.264, HEVC
   8 and 10 bit, VP8 and VP9 up to 2160p, MPEG-2 against the engine's own
   earlier output), 112 of 112 clip runs in 55 minutes of decoding them
   in a loop, and two codecs at once in 19 of 20 runs - the twentieth is
   the known timeout next to VP8 after a codec switch, which the same
   sequence shows at 432 MHz; that pair alone was bit-exact 20 of 20.

An hour of HEVC 2160p30 in Kodi at 600 MHz (a 60 s clip in a loop,
16.10.2026): 29.75 frames/s out of the engine, no 30 s window below
29.0, no timeout, no IOMMU fault, no eMMC error, the CPU and GPU zones
at most 68.4 and 70.6 degrees C. A quarter of an hour of H.264 2160p30:
28.85 frames/s (28.2 to 29.6), nothing in the log - H.264 at 2160p is at
the engine's limit even at 600 MHz.

Not measured: the HY300PRO-G-EU.
---
 .../staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c    | 34 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
index 2697fc774..e473dd583 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
@@ -565,6 +565,30 @@ int cedrus_hw_resume(struct device *device)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The H713's AV1 decoder, a separate core, runs from this same module clock
+ * and stalls into its own timeout above 432 MHz. While its node is enabled
+ * the H713 VE runs there; with the AV1 decoder off nothing holds it, and it
+ * keeps the H6's 600 MHz (at 432 MHz H.264 2160p decodes at 26 frames/s).
+ */
+#define CEDRUS_H713_AV1_MAX_RATE	432000000
+
+static unsigned long cedrus_mod_rate(const struct cedrus_variant *variant)
+{
+	struct device_node *np;
+	bool av1;
+
+	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("allwinner,sun50i-h713"))
+		return variant->mod_rate;
+
+	np = of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "allwinner,sun50i-h713-av1");
+	av1 = np && of_device_is_available(np);
+	of_node_put(np);
+
+	return av1 ? min_t(unsigned long, variant->mod_rate,
+			   CEDRUS_H713_AV1_MAX_RATE) : variant->mod_rate;
+}
+
 int cedrus_hw_probe(struct cedrus_dev *dev)
 {
 	const struct cedrus_variant *variant;
@@ -662,19 +686,13 @@ int cedrus_hw_probe(struct cedrus_dev *dev)
 		goto err_sram;
 	}
 
-	/*
-	 * The H713's AV1 decoder, a separate core, runs from this same module
-	 * clock and stalls into its own timeout above 432 MHz, so the H713 VE
-	 * runs there rather than at the H6's 600 MHz.
-	 */
-	ret = clk_set_rate(dev->mod_clk,
-			   of_machine_is_compatible("allwinner,sun50i-h713") ?
-			   432000000 : variant->mod_rate);
+	ret = clk_set_rate(dev->mod_clk, cedrus_mod_rate(variant));
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev->dev, "Failed to set clock rate\n");
 
 		goto err_sram;
 	}
+	dev_info(dev->dev, "module clock %lu Hz\n", clk_get_rate(dev->mod_clk));
 
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev->dev);
 	if (!pm_runtime_enabled(dev->dev)) {
